Root cause: The _keydown handler does not skip disabled tabs when calculating the next active element, causing focus to attempt to move to a disabled button which cannot receive focus, leaving focus unchanged and incorrectly marking the disabled tab as selected.

Repair strategy: Modify _keydown in tab.js to iterate over candidate next elements returned by getNextActiveElement, skipping any that are disabled per isDisabled, with a guard against infinite loops.

Expected accessibility effect: ArrowRight will now move focus to the next enabled tab (Billing) and update aria-selected accordingly, complying with keyboard navigation skipping disabled controls.

Functional risks: Potential infinite loop if all tabs are disabled (mitigated by break when returning to start). Change may affect behavior when upstream code expects disabled tabs to be selectable via arrow keys (unlikely). Ensure that tab activation logic still works for enabled tabs.

